		{
			dependencies: ["4181778D139B2C3C"]
			description: [
				"It's Gravlin' time."
				""
				"Hook up your &eautomatic cobblestone farm&r to your new &amillstones&r and bask in your endless gravel."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"As for the &bflint&r you can feed your new gravel into &aanother millstone&r to produce the flint. "
				""
				"While that does work to supply flint, this gets into a &6new concept&r that will be important to ensuring your factory hums along smoothly and avoid falling into &cpitfalls&r players &dnew to automation styled packs&r tend to run into."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"By feeding your gravel generator into a flint generator you introduce a &cbottleneck&r into your system. "
				""
				"If something ends up eating flint &etoo quickly&r other systems that rely on gravel will themselves be starved. "
				""
				"This can be solved by simply &6scaling up&r your gravel production to fully saturate your flint production. "
				""
				"Or you could design &b&l&n&oparallelized&r systems"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"In short when you design systems to be &bparallelized&r you are treating them as self contained units. "
				""
				"Why feed from the gravel maker to the flint maker when you can simply &6give the flint maker &n&l&oits own gravel maker&r? "
				""
				"That way both lines can produce without impacting each other!"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"This design concept for factories will help ensure &cbottlenecks&r are a lot &aeasier to resolve&r for very basic material production and will make for &asmoother expansions&r."
				""
				"Anyways thats probably the longest quest you've seen talking about making gravel, go on now, make it."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:gravel"
			id: "02755BE7FF325275"
			subtitle: "Designing good modules"
			tasks: [{
