		{
			dependencies: ["02755BE7FF325275"]
			description: [
				"With that concept of avoiding &cbottlenecks&r behind us we can start producing &bandesite&r!"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"With some &4lava&r in a basin your previously automated &eflint and gravel&r can be pressed into a fresh block of andesite."
				""
				"Oh but did you catch that about the recipe? It takes &a2&r flint and &a1&r gravel per craft."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Say hello to a &bnew concept&r in your factory endevors called &6&l&n&oratios!!!&r"
				""
				"&nWhat does that mean?&r Well certain recipes do not consume ingredients at the same pace, in our example andesite is &a2:1&r on it's &eflint:gravel&r consumption rate. "
				""
				"The hidden suggestion here is to simply &6double your flint production&r relative to your gravel production."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"And as an important point it's &cnot strictly necessary&r to math this out. "
				""
				"Sure you &ocould&r time how long each step makes and do a &6perfect ratio&r setup where &einput rates&r are exactly the same as &econsumption rate&r. "
				""
				"But... you are allowed to just eyeball it and go \"&aeh good enough&r\"."
				""
				"So long as you can spam the setups any setup will let your factory &4grow&r."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:andesite"
			id: "60A789A9FD9C1289"
			subtitle: "Ratios are important"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2E66033937FAB433"
				title: "I've always wanted to ratio a rock <3 18.7k"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Igneously Ingenious"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 10.0d
		}
