		{
			dependencies: ["16D01481957D30C3"]
			description: [
				"Twice blasted cobble call that &bSmooth Stone&r"
				""
				"While easy to make, automating it via create is &esurprisingly tricky&r. No matter the speed of the &bindustrial fan&r the actual processing time remains the same"
				""
				"This is tricky to deal with since &cunlike the &bMechanical Press&r items on belts won't stop to be processed. Items will simply pass by without having enough time to cook"
				""
				"There are three main ways to solve this (&cone of them being quite bad&r)"
				""
				"1) &nThe &cbad &fone&r: Items moving on belts will &aretain their cooking progress&r so long as the next belt tile is being blasted by &eanother fan&r. This creates the terrible solution of spamming the living hell out of fans for the full length of the belt. This method of course being &cworse the faster your belt is&r"
				""
				"2) &nThe &eok &fone&r: Instead of fan spam you can &aslow down a segment of belt&r to its minimum speed and point a &asingular fan to blow &bhorizontally &aacross the belt&r so that the items sit in the blasting stream long enough"
				""
				"3) &nThe &abest &fone&r: By investing in some &bbrass funnels&r or &bsmart chutes&r you can allow items to park at a &bdepot&r and only be sent off after they finish cooking by &6filtering the output&r component"
				""
				"You could also just, keep using furnaces I guess"
			]
			icon: "minecraft:smooth_stone"
			id: "5F863127930E520A"
			tasks: [{
