		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"1ECD32BB25F43FC0"
				"7667563D092228C1"
				"3A9D304009725ECF"
			]
			description: [
				"Now, with your &nlivingwood planks&r, &nlivisite alloy&r, and &npolished livingrock&r all automated you have an important decision before bulding your &detched living wood&r automation."
				""
				"&a&nAutocraft&r with &bcrafty crates&r and deal with &credstone&r."
				""
				"&4&nManually craft&r until &6mechanical crafters&r are available."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"This is an &n&6important decision&r to make because this recipe won't be the only one that needs crafting &o&ebefore&r you can create mechanical crafters."
				""
				"Specifically &d10 recipes&r are hard crafting-type requirements. One of which features an &cunstackable item&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The decision here is of &epersonal taste&r and &etolerance&r for manual tasks."
				""
				"And this decision is brought up because there will be several points where you may be tempted &cto put off automation&r until you can claw up to something better."
				""
				"Whether or not that is a good decision comes down to the time it will take to get to that \"&abetter thing&r\" while also &cforgoing the available option&r."
			]
			icon: "nyagibits_bytes:etched_living_wood"
			id: "1440D789406EF358"
			subtitle: "Decisions Decisions..."
			tasks: [{
				id: "105D977024CBD48C"
				title: "Pick your poison"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Comes With Recipe Eye Strain"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 13.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"7A974BCCA6882D04"
				"1440D789406EF358"
			]
			description: [
				"With both &betched living wood&r and &bandesite alloy&r being cranked out in the factory you can now enjoy &dandesite casings&r for &alittle to no personal involvement&r."
				""
				"Even &oless&r personal involvement if you chose to rush a &6deployer&r to finish the final step automatically. "
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Now here is an &n&aimportant shift in thinking&r that is vital to internalize moving forward."
				""
				"Recipe complexity ramps up incredibly fast beyond this point and it can be very easy to get &coverwhelmed&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The shift in thinking that can help quell those thoughts is this:"
				""
				"When a new thing is &aautomated&r, you can safely &bforget about all the previous steps&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To be more clear about this let's think about crafting &dGearboxes&r."
				""
				"Naturally when seeing the recipe you are needing to factor in crafting every single &esub-component&r since it was all done by hand."
				""
				"But now with &aautomated casings&r, a large chunk of that mental recipe tracking simply &ndoesn't need to happen anymore&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Now you have the luxury of &nonly thinking about crafting the &dcogs&r. Half the work is already done!"
				""
				"And if you &aautomate crafting the cogs well&r, that means any use-case that has a gearbox involved can be abstracted away to being \"&bbasically free&r\" or \"&birrelevant&r.\""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"In this way you can &dtighten your view&r to what is directly available to you while also freeing your brain from needing to worry about everything that comes before."
				""
				"After all when you make spaghetti at home you don't think about &emaking the noodles, sauce, cheese, and meat&r. You simply focus on making spaghetti."
				""
				"&l&o&bNow go and make your mechanical spaghetti sprawl&r!"
			]
			icon: "create:andesite_casing"
			id: "24F263BFA0B3056C"
			subtitle: "Less Labor = It's free* now!"
			tasks: [{
				id: "16A5B52FE76B8D2F"
				title: "Casings now on the cheap!"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Semi Manual Encasement"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 15.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6E61C014A48DD33A"]
			description: [
				"&6[W] To Ponder!&r"
				""
				"Botania is a tech mod, so it has a...well it can be a storage system, but it's more of a &ologistics&r system."
				"This is corporea, a system usually ignored by most due to requiring lategame resources. Not here, it is available very early on."
				""
				"To begin, make a &3Master Corporea Spark&r and a few &dCorporea Sparks&r."
				"Then, place the sparks over any inventory you want your corporea network to access."
				""
				"There must be one master spark somewhere in the network, but it will not be able to access an inventory itself."
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			icon: "botania:corporea_spark"
			id: "1BDC7381D6607E31"
			subtitle: "Massive retier?!"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7F1B5A8DA51F3038"
				title: "Zappy"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Best Storage System"
			x: 6.5d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1BDC7381D6607E31"]
			description: [
				"&6[W] To Ponder!&r"
				""
				"To connect to each other, &ntwo&r corporea sparks must be within &a8 blocks&r of eachother."
				""
				"To place sparks just to bridge a gap, you can use Corporea blocks and &bextend the network&r without needlessly adding more inventories."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"They're also perfect to place the &dmaster corporea spark&r on, since it can't access an inventory anyway, but is subject to the &esame placement restrictions&r."
				""
				"They also just look cool."
			]
			icon: "botania:corporea_block"
			id: "785652262D0F8C91"
			subtitle: "Rock but glittery"
			tasks: [{
				id: "651A918E5FCB1D7C"
				title: "Ourple"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Sparkly Block"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["785652262D0F8C91"]
			description: [
				"&6[W] To Ponder!&r"
				""
				"The &dCorporea Index&r is the main method for a player to withdraw items from a corporea network."
				""
				"To use it, &astand near it&r, and &astart talking&r &7(send a chat message)&r"
				"If the index is ready to use, you will see a &bcircle of sparks&r near it and a message while the chat box is open."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Instead of being sent out to the world, your message will be &einterpreted&r as a request and the item will be withdrawn from a connected inventory and pop out of the index."
				""
				"&nExample&r: Saying \"&d3 iron ingots&r\" will pop &d3 iron ingots&r from the network."
				"The full possibilities of requests are quite complex, so it's recommended to consult the lexica botania for more info."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"There is also special interactions with &6REI&r search! Make sure to check out &l&dAutomation and You! &f> &bThe Factory Must Grow&r"
			]
			icon: "botania:corporea_index"
			id: "616464677ADE6DB4"
			subtitle: "Ponder the or- uh, thingy"
			tasks: [{
				id: "09D40251E15BA879"
				title: "Hey! Gimmi!"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Speaking Your Demands"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["616464677ADE6DB4"]
			description: [
				"&6[W] To Ponder!&r"
				""
				"The &dCorporea Funnel&r is your main method of automatically transporting items with the corporea network."
				""
				"To use it, place it over an inventory, then place a &bcorporea spark&r on it to connect it to the network."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Place an &6item frame&r on the funnel, then put the item to request in the frame. "
				""
				"Rotate it to select the amount:"
				""
				"&lAmounts:&r 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 48, 64"
				""
				"Finally, give it a &credstone pulse&r to request the item and put it in the &ainventory underneath&r or, &7if there is a solid block under the funnel and an inventory below that&r, into that inventory through the block."
			]
			icon: "botania:corporea_funnel"
			id: "1829036099806630"
			subtitle: "Who even needs ae2?"
			tasks: [{
				id: "72C76F78F54F4570"
				title: "Telepathic Yoink"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Gimmi! But over here"
			x: 6.5d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["616464677ADE6DB4"]
			description: [
				"&6[W] To Ponder!&r"
				""
				"The Corporea Interceptor emits a &credstone pulse&r whenever a corporea request cannot be fulfilled."
				""
				"Placing an &6item frame&r on it will filter its action to just the item within the frame."
				""
				"The &credstone pulse&r can be used for anything, but the intended use is to activate a system that crafts the item."
				""
				"Deceptively useful for automation."
			]
			icon: "botania:corporea_interceptor"
			id: "4FDDF94EC02A0D02"
			subtitle: "Physically making your recipe tree"
			tasks: [{
				id: "21B47D2ED5678E91"
