		{
			dependencies: ["24F263BFA0B3056C"]
			description: [
				"Now to &ereel back the last quest&r, you should also do your best to &dmodularize&r your base."
				""
				"What does modularize mean? &aGood question&r!"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Early on you will be just &eslapping machines anywhere you can&r."
				""
				"And while this works short term, long term you end up getting some..."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Intensely &cdisfunctional&r spaghetti..."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/absolute_mess.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"The real issue with this is that, if any one machine starts to &efall behind&r, expanding it becomes a nightmare if not outright &cimpossible&r without gutting the whole thing."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"That is why &aexpandability&r is something to consider when building chunks of factory."
				""
				"In this case we will be stealing a concept from &l&6Factorio&r called \"&bThe Main Bus&r.\""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Here we have a &6cobblestone&r generator, &cgravel&r, &eflint&r, and &aandesite&r being made. &bColor-coded by belt&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/main_bus_example.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Following the orange path we see it come from the &6cobblestone&r generator &otowards&r a main belt moving to the left."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/bus_cobble.png width:185 height:116 align:center}"
				""
				"Then a junction is made wherever &6cobblestone&r is needed for a recipe. In this case &6cobblestone&r -> &cgravel&r via millstones."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"After this recipe is done the &cgravel&r is again brought to the main line of belts and sent to the left."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/bus_gravel.png width:185 height:116 align:center}"
				""
				"Here we see it has two junctions, one to send it to millstones to make &eflint&r, and another junction to send it to &aandesite&r production."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Following a &bsimilar&r factory scheme as this is a fairly easy way to &aendlessly expand individual production blocks&r while having clear visuals on production points and end points."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/bus_structure.png width:185 height:116 align:center}"
				""
				"And naturally this is a tight clustering to fit it into a screenshot. "
				""
				"You can get very &bcreative&r with actual positioning of your modules. Go make some beautiful and functional builds!"
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			icon: "botania:auto_crafting_halo"
