		{
			dependencies: [
				"1829036099806630"
				"56BAD950091D55D1"
			]
			description: [
				"&6[W] To Ponder!&r"
				""
				"Botania's &aCrafty Crate&r is a &6very cheap&r and &6very fast&r autocrafter for any default 3x3 recipes"
				""
				"So whats the catch?"
				""
				"The crafty crate must take in a recipe &d1 item at a time&r in the &dcorrect sequence&r to fill up its own inventory and only then will the recipe process"
				""
				"The resulting item will be &aejected&r from the bottom of the crate either into the world or into a valid inventory"
				""
				"This means that if your &credstone messes up&r and items enter out of order the crafty crate will &cchoke&r and nothing will pass through"
				""
				"The &aspeed and reliability&r of your crafting setups is &b100% up to you&r, and how tightly you can engineer the sequence of items entering the crate and extraction of said items, &da pure skill check&r"
			]
			icon: "botania:crafty_crate"
			id: "607E9B99520A22A2"
			subtitle: "Molecular assemblers are locked to tier 3, get good"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0754A61387637A99"
				title: "This is basically a vanilla crafter, but harder"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Autocrafting, But With A Skill Check"
			x: 6.5d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["607E9B99520A22A2"]
			description: [
				"You may notice some recipes have &eempty slots&r between items like buckets or shears"
				""
				"To do crafts like this with the crafty crate you'll need to get your hands on a set of &aCrafting Placeholders&r"
				""
				"As the name implies these are items that can be slotted into a crafty crate but &6act as an empty space&r, allowing any following items to slot into their correct spots"
				""
				"When the craft completes these placeholders are &aejected from the crate&r along with the completed craft"
				""
				"There are also &dCrafting Patterns&r you can craft from placeholders that, when right-clicked onto a crate, outright &bblock a designated set of slots&r from the crate"
			]
			icon: "botania:placeholder"
